commit ad10e7dddbbec1fe9c1d82db2650516ca1407adb
Author: Goutham Kumar <goutham.kumar@blubridge.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 10:19:51 2026 +0000

    loss: fp32 loss scalar, dtype-aware vector loads, fp32 grad_output (Bugs A/B/C) + ignore_index/denominator
    
    Bug A: the loss scalar and every intermediate loss buffer are fp32
    (they were narrowed to the logits dtype 3 times).
    Bug B: 16-byte vector loads use LossVec<T> = 16/sizeof(T) elements
    instead of a hardcoded 4, plus a scalar tail for vocab % width, so
    bf16 logits no longer fault (misaligned address) or overrun the
    gradient row.
    Bug C: grad_output is const float*.
    
    sparse_cross_entropy_loss(logits, targets, ignore_index = -1,
    denom = nullptr): existing 2-argument callers are unchanged.
    Supersedes a407093's AccT partial fix in LossKernels.cu (fp32
    partials but a bf16 final store, which overflows to Inf once the
    summed loss reaches 65536).
    
    Validated on H200 with bluscript_zero_ckpt, BLU_BF16_LOGITS=0 vs 1
    (this fix makes =1 usable; before, it crashed at step 0): 20/20 steps.
    At B=4, 1 GPU:
      live peak      95,038 -> 90,322 MiB (-4,716)
      reserved peak 104,904 -> 99,028 MiB (-5,876)  (what nvidia-smi shows)
      identical over 4 runs on 2 days
      loss-path DRAM traffic -75%; loss within run-to-run noise
    Expected at B=8: about -9.2 GiB live per GPU.

